1
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:24,260
Those with no money, come to my place.

2
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,960
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

3
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:36,040
Look, the blue sky and white clouds.

4
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:36,460
me

5
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,060
Somehow it'll work out, I guess.

6
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:46,880
Fuhahahahaha

7
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:59,900
Those with no job, come to my place.

8
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

9
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:11,980
Look, even the red sky is burning.

10
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:18,260
Somehow it'll work out eventually, right?

11
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:23,540
You get it, right? I get it, I get it.

12
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,460
If you understand, follow me without a word.

13
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:42,680
Thank goodness, Kei-chan.

14
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:46,760
My car's in for inspection, so I was
just about to take the train to work.

15
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:49,000
What a coincidence, Reiko-san.

16
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:51,940
On days like this,
coincidences tend to pile up.

17
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:54,460
What's wrong?

18
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:57,320
I think I saw Senpai in the trash just now.

19
00:01:58,340 --> 00:01:59,300
I'll go take a look.

20
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:00,480
I'm coming too.

21
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:02,600
He seems to be alive.

22
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:06,800
Well, it really is Senpai.

23
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:09,180
Senpai, please wake up.

24
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:11,860
It's nothing, really.

25
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:12,240
Senpai.

26
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:16,280
What? You! Barging into people's
homes without permission!

27
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:18,800
This is a garbage collection point,
you know.

28
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:23,140
I see. I must have gotten
drunk and passed out here.

29
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:26,680
I was at my twentieth New
Year's party until dawn.

30
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:29,080
New Year's party? It's already April!

31
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:33,840
But why is the uniform so tattered?

32
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:35,960
Don't you remember?

33
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:37,620
The dog's injuries.

34
00:02:37,620 --> 00:02:40,700
Oh right, I think I fought three dogs.

35
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:42,940
Your behavior is completely reckless.

36
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:46,660
By the way, why are you two
wearing plain clothes to work?

37
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:49,640
Oh come on, senpai, did you forget?

38
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:52,940
The Chief said we should come
in plain clothes tomorrow.

39
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:54,700
That's right.

40
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:58,280
Perfect timing.
Change into the plain clothes in the locker.

41
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:00,220
Let's just throw this one away.

42
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:02,060
You're throwing away your uniform?

43
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:05,820
What? It just means I'll get a
new one within two or three days.

44
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:09,560
Kindly thief.

45
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:18,000
The reason I've had you all gather
here in plainclothes is none other than

46
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,460
lately, there's been a string of burglaries
within the Katsushika station's jurisdiction.

47
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:25,800
So I want you to patrol in plainclothes

48
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:28,440
and keep an eye out for anyone suspicious.

49
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:29,980
Hey, Ryoozu!

50
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:33,960
Don't "huh" me, you idiot!
Are you even listening?

51
00:03:34,540 --> 00:03:38,280
I'm listening! Don't shout right in my ear.

52
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:40,340
It's pounding in my head.

53
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:43,660
You looked like you were sleeping on your feet,
so I woke you up.

54
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:47,760
Listen, just because you're in plainclothes doesn't mean you can slack off,
or you'll answer to me.

55
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:50,460
I get it, I get it.

56
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:19,740
Just as I thought, nobody's home.

57
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:22,400
This is terrible.

58
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:24,920
There's not even a place to step.

59
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:27,880
What a mess.

60
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:28,320
Damn it.

61
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:32,600
Here too?

62
00:04:40,260 --> 00:04:43,300
What a slob.

63
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:43,960
Ugh.

64
00:04:54,430 --> 00:04:56,140
Damn it.

65
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:04,280
I just feel uneasy unless I sleep like this,
you know.

66
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,880
Now I can get to work with peace of mind.

67
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:11,000
Touched?

68
00:05:11,860 --> 00:05:13,200
Uh-oh, someone's coming.

69
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:19,860
Yachi-yachi-yachi.

70
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:21,900
Ber-ber-ber.

71
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:22,540
Idiot.

72
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:25,700
What? Is your diaper wet?

73
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:27,620
You went and did it,
you went and did it, you went and did it.

74
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:31,840
I knew it, it's wet.

75
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:33,520
Hold on a second, you know.

76
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:37,820
There, that's better.

77
00:05:38,420 --> 00:05:39,560
Don't cry anymore, okay?

78
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:43,580
Whoa, this isn't the time
to be changing diapers!

79
00:05:43,580 --> 00:05:44,980
Hey, Mr. Yamashita!

80
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:47,420
I'm here to collect for the newspaper.

81
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:51,080
The door wasn't locked?

82
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:54,720
I knocked, but there was no answer, so...

83
00:05:56,140 --> 00:05:56,580
Are you really that upset?

84
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:58,320
Could I have the newspaper payment, please?

85
00:05:58,920 --> 00:05:59,800
Two months' worth.

86
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:02,220
I'm the one who has to pay?

87
00:06:02,740 --> 00:06:04,100
Of course you are.

88
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:06,380
Who else is going to pay for it?

89
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:08,560
Th-that's true, I guess.

90
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:10,300
Damn it.

91
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:11,940
Thank you very much.

92
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:16,540
Damn it, why do I have to pay?

93
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:20,320
The laundry!

94
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:27,900
Why does it always end up like this?

95
00:06:28,340 --> 00:06:29,620
Geez, what a useless guy I am.

96
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,840
I left the laundry out, didn't I?

97
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:37,000
S-they're back!

98
00:06:43,460 --> 00:06:45,700
It's raining, and I'm sleepy,

99
00:06:45,750 --> 00:06:48,040
on a day like this,
tomorrow's a day off too, right?

100
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:51,480
As for me, I'm done for today.

101
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:57,040
Want to knock back a drink
to keep the hangover away?

102
00:06:57,860 --> 00:06:58,900
Here you go.

103
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:03,700
I feel like I've been brought back to life.

104
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:08,480
What's with the pitiful sigh?

105
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:11,540
I don't know what happened,

106
00:07:11,540 --> 00:07:14,340
but keep that face up and even
the moon will run away from you.

107
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:16,060
Yeah, that's exactly it.

108
00:07:16,570 --> 00:07:18,240
I'm such a total sucker for other people.

109
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:21,140
Everything I do just backfires on me.

110
00:07:23,060 --> 00:07:25,060
I'm confident in my skills, though.

111
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:30,140
But I'm such a coward that
nothing has ever worked out for me.

112
00:07:30,140 --> 00:07:32,680
Don't mope.
Where there's a will, there's a way.

113
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:34,680
Where there's a will, there's a way?

114
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:38,840
Yeah. A man needs guts,
and sometimes he has to brazen it out.

115
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:40,780
Brazen it out?

116
00:07:41,340 --> 00:07:43,480
Rather than worrying, just take action.

117
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:46,820
Throw the door wide open
and go straight for it.

118
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:51,620
But I always get close to the good part,
and then something gets in the way.

119
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:54,020
Interference comes with the territory.

120
00:07:54,020 --> 00:07:58,820
But when you overcome it and succeed,
the joy is all the greater.

121
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:02,180
I see. Well, that's convincing.

122
00:08:02,180 --> 00:08:03,880
I should take a leaf out of your book.

123
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:07,640
That's right. If you're afraid of failing,
you'll never become a big shot.

124
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:09,460
Hm?

125
00:08:11,360 --> 00:08:12,380
Uh-oh, this is bad.

126
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:17,620
Gah! That flash I just caught sight of...
could it be Ryō-2?

127
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:30,260
Excuse me! Was there a man with a crew
cut and joined eyebrows here just now?

128
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:38,620
There was a man, but he had brown hair and a general's beard.
He just left out the back, the one with brown hair.

129
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:40,320
Guess it was a different person.

130
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:42,800
My apologies.

131
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:48,820
Phew, that saved me.

132
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:50,460
You're a good man.

133
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:51,500
I owe you one.

134
00:08:51,500 --> 00:08:53,200
I'm Ryotsu.

135
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:54,520
The name's Nameraa.

136
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:57,180
Sir, you're surely in that line of work,
aren't you?

137
00:08:58,800 --> 00:08:59,600
Well, yeah.

138
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:01,180
You've got the presence for it.

139
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:03,360
You must be someone of note.

140
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:05,900
Well, around here,
the only ones who don't know me

141
00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:06,860
are outsiders, you see.

142
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:13,640
I'll follow Ryo-chan's example and
go all in on a one-shot test of guts.

143
00:09:14,160 --> 00:09:15,960
That's the spirit! Good luck.

144
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:19,300
I'll do it.
This time I'll succeed, you'll see.

145
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:26,520
Nothing was taken, the laundry was brought in,
and it was even ironed.

146
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:29,320
They say the dishes were washed neatly too.

147
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:32,460
There really are some strange people around,
aren't there?

148
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,680
Did anything happen on Kei-chan's side?

149
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:37,300
No, nothing in particular.

150
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:41,200
I wonder how today's going?
Is he doing his job properly?

151
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:43,580
Well, it's him, after all.

152
00:09:44,060 --> 00:09:46,620
I'll do it, I'll really do it this time!

153
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:49,970
Moving day!

154
00:09:50,020 --> 00:09:53,680
Right, I'll blend in with the helpers.

155
00:09:55,540 --> 00:09:58,520
Here, pass that over here, thank you.

156
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:11,280
They're all heavy things.

157
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:14,060
Isn't there anything
lighter and more valuable?

158
00:10:18,420 --> 00:10:19,840
This hanging scroll, then.

159
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:21,160
No.

160
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:25,640
Did I scare you too much?

161
00:10:26,380 --> 00:10:27,680
What happened?

162
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:29,520
Are you helping with the move?

163
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:31,740
Do you know them?

164
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:34,020
No, not at all.

165
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:35,280
I see.

166
00:10:35,280 --> 00:10:35,960
No, no.

167
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:38,980
Well, helping out without anyone knowing,
what a commendable fellow.

168
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:42,880
Damn! That noisy one's coming again.

169
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:47,840
Why are you hiding too?

170
00:10:49,020 --> 00:10:51,260
Well, I just got caught up with Ryo-san.

171
00:10:55,740 --> 00:10:56,540
He's gone.

172
00:10:56,540 --> 00:10:57,140
Yes.

173
00:10:58,180 --> 00:11:01,700
Well, I'm off.
Let's have a drink again sometime.

174
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:02,280
Y-yes.

175
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:06,360
Right, I should stop dawdling too.

176
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:09,300
Let's get to it.

177
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:13,520
Everyone, take a break.

178
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:22,620
We finally did it, it's a success!

179
00:11:23,940 --> 00:11:26,200
What's this? It's a jar of pickled plums.

180
00:11:27,540 --> 00:11:29,540
Why would anyone steal something like this?

181
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:31,920
And look at me, what a useless guy I am.

182
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:36,120
Ryotsu must be slacking off, I'm sure of it.

183
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:45,760
Damn it, if they see me with this hungover face,
we're in trouble.

184
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:51,960
Even so,
is this how they're keeping watch on Kiss?

185
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:54,660
I can't tell if they're
worried about Ryotsu or not.

186
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,460
Thanks, everyone, for your hard work.

187
00:11:57,920 --> 00:12:00,480
Just give it one more push at the new place,
will you?

188
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:01,240
Yes, Chief.

189
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:02,360
Leave it to me.

190
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,340
Hey, where's the pickled plum jar?

191
00:12:09,620 --> 00:12:11,980
Don't you have it?

192
00:12:12,060 --> 00:12:14,840
I thought you had it. I don't know.

193
00:12:16,460 --> 00:12:18,580
Maybe they loaded it onto the truck.

194
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:22,840
Why would anyone bother
with a pickled plum jar?

195
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:44,880
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

196
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:49,240
Apparently, it's the pickled plum jar. Is
the pickled plum jar really that important?

197
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:53,220
Inside it is our entire fortune,
30 million yen.

198
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:55,760
What, 30 million?

199
00:13:01,580 --> 00:13:02,380
It's money!

200
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:09,360
No good, the amount is too much. It's scary.

201
00:13:11,820 --> 00:13:13,720
No, no way!

202
00:13:14,340 --> 00:13:16,240
No way, not him...

203
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,960
Anyway, let's go back and check.

204
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:22,520
What if that money isn't there?

205
00:13:25,120 --> 00:13:26,700
You dropped something.

206
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:29,720
Hey, you! That...

207
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:34,900
You dropped this notepad.

208
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:36,480
Thank you.

209
00:13:39,540 --> 00:13:40,620
It's here!

210
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:44,760
You saved us. How can we ever thank you?

211
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:47,640
No, thanks are unnecessary.

212
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:49,200
Well then, I'll be going.

213
00:13:50,920 --> 00:13:53,360
Wait, what a man without greed!

214
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:56,180
Why don't I take it in his place?

215
00:13:56,180 --> 00:13:58,420
It has nothing to do with you!

216
00:13:58,420 --> 00:13:59,600
Yeah, no good.

217
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:28,500
 no,
no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no

218
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:31,400
Let's just grab the stuff and skedaddle.

219
00:14:43,680 --> 00:14:45,000
Mister, who are you?

220
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:46,040
What do you want?

221
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:50,640
I'm a friend of your father.

222
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:53,000
I was in the neighborhood,
so I came to see him.

223
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,960
Dad's dead.

224
00:14:55,380 --> 00:14:55,580
What?

225
00:14:56,160 --> 00:14:57,300
R-right.

226
00:14:57,300 --> 00:15:01,480
Oh yes! On your mom's side, too, a cousin
of a cousin's cousin's neighbor's kid is...

227
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:04,360
Ahaha! Mom,
are you having a house-sitting party?

228
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:07,160
Mom's in the hospital, she's sick.

229
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:12,740
Just taking shelter from the rain.

230
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:14,620
Whoa! Chief!

231
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:21,800
I knew it! What do you think patrol means?!

232
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:25,660
No, Chief, you see,
this is part of our stakeout.

233
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:29,280
Forget the patrol.

234
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:31,640
Go check on the Tanakas' place.

235
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:35,160
Their mother's in the hospital,
so it's just the kids there.

236
00:15:35,160 --> 00:15:40,480
I see.

237
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:42,440
So it's only the kids, then.

238
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:46,620
The wind's picking up quite a bit.

239
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:48,920
Hey, is your house okay?

240
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:50,320
Yeah.

241
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:51,780
It's a real dump, after all.

242
00:15:53,060 --> 00:15:53,820
Excuse me.

243
00:15:54,820 --> 00:15:58,260
Is it leaking?

244
00:15:58,780 --> 00:16:01,700
You're here again, Ryo-san.

245
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:06,420
I see, you're here too
because it's just the kids

246
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:10,560
Yes, well,
great minds think alike, don't they?

247
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:18,180
Things are really getting serious now.
Hey, is everyone here? Everyone, assemble!

248
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:19,780
Ichiro, the eldest son.

249
00:16:19,780 --> 00:16:21,220
Matsuko, the eldest daughter.

250
00:16:21,220 --> 00:16:22,620
Jiro, the second son.

251
00:16:22,620 --> 00:16:23,800
Takeko, the second daughter.

252
00:16:23,800 --> 00:16:25,300
Umeko, the youngest.

253
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:27,220
Saburo isn't here.

254
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:28,960
What? Where is he?

255
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:31,220
I think he was in the kitchen a moment ago.

256
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:38,080
He went and knocked over the pickle jar!

257
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:39,720
He's covered in nukamiso!

258
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:42,340
That's what you get for
playing on something like this.

259
00:16:43,020 --> 00:16:44,340
I'll go look for some clothes.

260
00:16:44,340 --> 00:16:47,060
You wash this one in the bathroom.

261
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:54,880
I wonder when they plan on working.

262
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:02,460
And while you're at it,
get all these kids into the bath.

263
00:17:02,840 --> 00:17:04,520
Then we need to fix the roof.

264
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:06,200
Fix the roof?

265
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:08,020
The antenna's about to fall over.

266
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:09,980
The carport's going to come down too.

267
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:10,880
See ya.

268
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:25,220
The rain and wind are awful, aren't they.

269
00:17:25,220 --> 00:17:26,020
Really.

270
00:17:26,020 --> 00:17:27,920
Good work, everyone.

271
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:31,820
I hear the habitual burglar was caught
in the neighboring station's jurisdiction.

272
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,260
That's a relief.

273
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:35,060
Is Senpai still not here?

274
00:17:35,060 --> 00:17:38,220
I gave that guy a special assignment.

275
00:17:38,220 --> 00:17:39,680
Special assignment?

276
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:45,520
Hold it down more firmly!

277
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:47,140
But my feet keep slipping.

278
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:48,620
So what? That's nothing.

279
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:52,800
Okay, tighten that wire on your side more.

280
00:17:52,800 --> 00:17:53,940
Y-yes.

281
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:05,740
Lift it up.

282
00:18:05,740 --> 00:18:07,020
Okay, that's good.

283
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:08,620
Next, the riverbank.

284
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:12,580
You're pretty handy, aren't you?

285
00:18:13,780 --> 00:18:16,820
By the way, Ryo-san, when are we doing it?

286
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:18,820
When?

287
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:21,680
After the kids are asleep.

288
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:24,100
Right, of course. Naturally.

289
00:18:25,180 --> 00:18:25,900
Yeah, yeah.

290
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:27,900
We need to fix the roof, too.

291
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:35,780
Yay!

292
00:18:35,860 --> 00:18:37,920
I lost again!

293
00:18:38,300 --> 00:18:39,880
Uncle, you're weak!

294
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:42,400
Hey, is the food still not ready?

295
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:44,180
Yes, coming right -

296
00:18:45,180 --> 00:18:46,820
Hotpot? Nice.

297
00:18:46,820 --> 00:18:48,060
Coming!

298
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:50,800
I just made it with
whatever was on hand, though.

299
00:18:54,260 --> 00:18:55,660
How is it? Tasty?

300
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:58,500
Uncle, seconds please.

301
00:18:58,500 --> 00:18:59,200
Me too!

302
00:18:59,300 --> 00:19:00,560
I'm first!

303
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:03,180
Alright, alright,
one at a time, one at a time.

304
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:08,100
Well, looks like everyone's asleep.

305
00:19:08,580 --> 00:19:08,800
Yes.

306
00:19:10,180 --> 00:19:11,280
Alright, let's get to it.

307
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:23,960
But the world really is unfair, isn't it?

308
00:19:25,460 --> 00:19:30,040
No matter how hard you work honestly,
life never gets any better.

309
00:19:31,780 --> 00:19:35,900
while only the people who cheat and
scheme get to enjoy the good life.

310
00:19:35,900 --> 00:19:39,140
But a man should live with a positive outlook,
you know.

311
00:19:39,600 --> 00:19:42,780
With nothing but your bare body,
you can do anything.

312
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:44,660
You think so?

313
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:50,460
But before complaining, what matters is
having the spirit to change the world yourself.

314
00:19:50,460 --> 00:19:55,020
Born a man in this world, if you don't
do something, a man has no worth, right?

315
00:19:57,020 --> 00:19:58,380
Yeah, as a man, I suppose.

316
00:19:58,380 --> 00:19:58,720
Mm.

317
00:20:01,880 --> 00:20:03,520
I'm going to bed now.

318
00:20:23,060 --> 00:20:24,320
Five thousand yen

319
00:20:27,340 --> 00:20:28,740
A man needs guts.

320
00:20:28,740 --> 00:20:31,000
Sometimes you've got to brazen it out.

321
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:33,900
Brazen it out.

322
00:20:36,600 --> 00:20:38,880
Rather than worrying, all you can do is act.

323
00:20:39,580 --> 00:20:41,380
Just act.

324
00:20:42,860 --> 00:20:46,300
Even among fellow cops,
it's eat or be eaten.

325
00:20:51,060 --> 00:20:51,860
A cop.

326
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:54,420
A cop with this face?

327
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:56,940
No matter how you look at it,
I've got the bearing of a criminal.

328
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:05,900
Where are you going, mister?

329
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:09,080
I'm just going to the bathroom.

330
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:11,120
I'm coming too, take me with you!

331
00:21:11,940 --> 00:21:13,180
Well, I guess there's no helping it.

332
00:21:20,260 --> 00:21:21,700
Let's go while we can.

333
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:28,960
The sewage is overflowing.

334
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:36,280
Mister?

335
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:45,980
If it overflows here,

336
00:21:45,980 --> 00:21:47,620
these kids will...

337
00:21:51,220 --> 00:21:52,380
I'm...

338
00:21:52,380 --> 00:21:53,220
I'm...

339
00:21:53,220 --> 00:21:54,920
Mister...

340
00:21:55,860 --> 00:21:57,360
Mister, where are you?

341
00:21:59,840 --> 00:22:01,400
Mister...

342
00:22:13,120 --> 00:22:14,480
Uncle

343
00:22:15,100 --> 00:22:17,500
Are you okay? You weren't hurt?

344
00:22:18,120 --> 00:22:21,580
Yeah, because you disappeared, Uncle.

345
00:22:25,080 --> 00:22:25,900
Uncle

346
00:22:25,900 --> 00:22:30,940
Are you going somewhere, mister?

347
00:22:30,940 --> 00:22:32,400
Don't go away.

348
00:22:32,900 --> 00:22:35,140
Sorry, I'm not going anywhere.

349
00:22:35,540 --> 00:22:37,280
I'll stay with you the whole time, okay?

350
00:22:37,660 --> 00:22:38,020
Yeah.

351
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:44,620
I knew you'd come back.

352
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:46,340
Ryo-san

353
00:22:46,800 --> 00:22:49,220
You knew who I really was?

354
00:22:50,300 --> 00:22:51,560
Who I really am, you mean?

355
00:22:51,560 --> 00:22:55,520
Well, a kind uncle who loves kids, right?

356
00:22:56,700 --> 00:22:57,820
Ryo-san

357
00:22:59,980 --> 00:23:01,335
Come on, in you go, in you go.

358
00:23:01,385 --> 00:23:04,040
Standing out there like that,
you'll catch a cold.

359
00:23:04,040 --> 00:23:04,740
Yes.

360
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:10,880
Good thing it wasn't anything serious.

361
00:23:17,120 --> 00:23:19,800
New uniforms really do feel good,
don't they.

362
00:23:22,120 --> 00:23:28,340
About the other day, thanks. I've finally
found a job that's just right for me.

363
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:38,220
A government home helper, is it? Yes, I never realized
there was a job that gives such a sense of purpose.

364
00:23:39,280 --> 00:23:42,800
I see, it really suits you.
Do your best. Yes.

365
00:23:43,740 --> 00:23:45,100
Time to go home, okay?

366
00:23:45,100 --> 00:23:51,240
I don't see him around much,
but you two seem really close, Ryo-san.

367
00:23:51,240 --> 00:23:55,020
Oh, he's just a drinking buddy.

368
00:24:15,100 --> 00:24:18,680
Na na na na, na na na na

369
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:24,200
to those who go all-out on looks alone

370
00:24:24,200 --> 00:24:27,380
I probably don't want to be like that

371
00:24:27,380 --> 00:24:31,980
if you're dawdling around the corner

372
00:24:31,980 --> 00:24:34,300
the moon has slipped away

373
00:24:34,300 --> 00:24:38,060
because now isn't everything

374
00:24:38,060 --> 00:24:42,520
don't get too worked up

375
00:24:42,520 --> 00:24:46,260
even if you fudge a little with lies

376
00:24:46,260 --> 00:24:50,420
every now and then, while helping someone

377
00:24:50,420 --> 00:24:53,430
Baby, do you know me?

378
00:24:53,480 --> 00:24:54,500
toward tomorrow

379
00:24:54,500 --> 00:24:56,640
what a great spirit

380
00:24:57,820 --> 00:25:01,780
Silly or not, we'll do what we've gotta do.

381
00:25:01,780 --> 00:25:04,220
A cute, spirited attitude.

382
00:25:04,220 --> 00:25:07,620
What's hard to understand

383
00:25:08,780 --> 00:25:11,100
is just how we want to appear.

384
00:25:12,860 --> 00:25:17,360
Better than a makeover, right?

385
00:25:19,200 --> 00:25:24,940
Nan-nan-nan-nan-nan-nan-nan-nan-nan-nan

386
00:25:28,160 --> 00:25:30,980
Over there is Kameari!

387
00:25:32,080 --> 00:25:34,380
Well, surely it's Kameari!

388
00:25:34,380 --> 00:25:39,360
Everyone, come on over to our town!

389
00:25:40,260 --> 00:25:40,980
Thank you.

390
00:25:42,520 --> 00:25:43,780
Thanks for watching.

